# Security Policy

## Supported versions

This project is pre-1.0 (`0.1.0`). Security fixes land on `main`; there is no
separate maintenance branch at this stage. The release automation can publish
versioned images, but consumers should verify that a tag exists in GHCR before
using the examples in this repository.

## Reporting a vulnerability

Please do not open a public GitHub issue for security vulnerabilities.

Instead, report it privately via [GitHub Security
Advisories](https://github.com/bassemZohdy/specs-agent-platform/security/advisories/new)
for this repository, or by emailing bassem.zohdy@gmail.com with a description
of the issue, steps to reproduce, and its potential impact.

You should expect an initial response within 5 business days. We will work
with you to confirm the issue, develop a fix, and coordinate disclosure
timing before any public write-up.

## Scope

Relevant areas for this platform include (non-exhaustive):

- Document loading and parsing (`open_agent_core.loader`,
  `open_agent_core.workflow.loader`, and `open_agent_core.agent_spec.loader`) —
  especially handling of untrusted YAML/JSON application bundles.
- API authentication and request handling in the LangGraph and ADK runners
  (`open_agent_lang.runner`, `open_agent_adk.runner`).
- MCP process/tool invocation (`open_agent_lang.mcp`, `open_agent_adk.mcp`).
- Checkpoint persistence (`open_agent_core.persistence`).

Issues in third-party dependencies should generally be reported upstream,
but feel free to flag them here too if they materially affect this project's
deployments.

## Published container images

Release images are scanned before release tags are published and have BuildKit
OCI SBOM and provenance attestations attached to their GHCR digests. Inspect a
deployed image by digest rather than relying on a moving tag:

```bash
docker buildx imagetools inspect \
  ghcr.io/bassemzohdy/specs-agent-lang@sha256:REPLACE_WITH_DIGEST
```

See [Container images](docs/containers.md) for the equivalent ADK command and
deployment guidance. GitHub artifact attestations are deferred because they do
not support this private personal repository. Report a suspected compromised
image or OCI attestation using the private vulnerability-reporting process.
